# Backpressure decision card canonical matrix golden
# br-uwih7 + br-6bgp1 + br-817cba87c
# Format:
#   <priority>:<shape>  | state=<S> action=<A> score=<I> fallback=<F>
# - state: classified backpressure_state from telemetry
# - action: selected action (admit/admit_with_warning/delay/shed/cancel_low_priority/fallback_static_policy)
# - score: selected_loss_score (deterministic; weight refactor → per-row number diff)
# - fallback: trigger when fallback path fires; 'none' otherwise
#
# Cells:
#   4 priorities × 6 telemetry shapes = 24 admission rows
#   3 fallback rows (missing telemetry, coverage drift, replay mismatch)
#
# Findings observable in this matrix (use as operator dashboard guide):
#   - admit_with_warning IS load-bearing in production: it fires for
#     Critical/High/Normal at cpu_saturated. Operators MUST surface
#     the tracing::warn! the host integration emits (br-uwih7 fix).
#   - Low priority falls into cancel_low_priority three of six shapes
#     (queue_congested, memory_pressure, warning_band) — the loss
#     matrix's priority_factor (Low=1) makes this the lowest-loss
#     action when shedding is needed.
#   - Critical never picks shed under any non-fallback shape except
#     memory_pressure, where shed scores 2.07e9 — verifying the
#     priority-shed-monotonicity property (Critical is most-protected).

